# What `project/readme.py`, `project/metadata.py`, `project/docs.py` and `project/run_skill.py` rendered
# before the standing text in them moved out to `assets/`, as SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of each file.
#
# The move is only worth doing if it changed nothing a project receives, and "generate before and after"
# cannot be run across one commit. So these were captured at 074aa35, the commit slice 16.4 was written on
# top of, by the matrix `tests/test_project_pages.py` describes, and the new path has to reproduce them
# exactly. Anyone can take the same reading: check out 074aa35, put that module beside this file, and run
#
#     PYTHONPATH=src:tests python3 -c "import sys, test_project_pages; sys.stdout.write(test_project_pages.lines())"
#
# and compare it with the lines below. The module that prints them changes nothing the generator does, so
# the reading is the same whether it is taken at 074aa35 or at the commit that added it.
#
# Fifty-six combinations: six application sets — a repository the keel made none of, one service, a service
# with a browser app, two services on two rungs with two browser apps, a service with no inbound transport,
# and that service with a browser app beside it — against both profiles and four target-and-shape answers,
# plus the delivery layout for the set whose pages read it.
# `<digest>  <apps>/<profile>/<target>-<shape>/<delivery>  <path>`.
#
# The sixth set was added after the first five were recorded, because it is the only one that reaches the
# run skill's no-transport section and the README's run block with no service to start. Its rows were read
# the same way, at 074aa35 restored from the history — and re-reading the other five there reproduced the
# lines already here byte for byte, which is what makes appending to a record safe rather than a second
# reading of a moved target.
#
# A deliberate edit to one of these pages changes these lines, which is the point: the diff a reviewer has
# to see is the prose, and this file is what refuses to let it pass unseen.
